    "title": "Wednesday's Health Report: Keeping babies safe as they sleep - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WBRZ Staff ,\n4 hours ago Keeping babies safe isn't just a day job at night, some parents may unknowing be putting their child at risk. In 2022, there were about 3,700 sudden unexpected infant deaths in the United States. More than 1,500 were from sudden infant death syndrome, or SIDS, more than 1,100 were from unknown causes and more than 1,000 deaths came from accidental causes. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
